Guest fixes:
- flushMappedPersistentBuffers: indices are an offset when an element array buffer is bound,
  reading them as a pointer crashed
- buffer targets without a slot (GL_COPY_READ_BUFFER, ...) no longer index past vao->buffer
- glPixelStorei keeps the unpack alignment/skips and the pack state
- glReadPixels places the tightly packed rows from the host with the pack row length,
  alignment and skips
- glReadPixels into a pixel pack buffer waits for the host, the buffer is mapped and read
  without asking the host, so the pixels could be read before the host had written them
- glGetTexImage/glGetCompressedTexImage write into the pixel pack buffer when one is bound
  (pixels is an offset then, writing to it crashed)
- glVertexAttribPointer strides for packed vertex formats
- glXCreateNewContext passes a NULL attribute list, which crashed glXCreateContextAttribsARB

